# We found the exact Java code responsible

Using **JADX**, we traced the error into:

```text
PairingProblemChecker.problemCheckAfterPairing()
```

The original method was essentially:

```java
public static final Problem problemCheckAfterPairing(
        WearableDevice wearableDevice,
        BluetoothDevice bluetoothDevice,
        boolean isConnectedSAKInsecure,
        FragmentActivity activity) {

    da.i.e(wearableDevice, "wearableDevice");
    da.i.e(bluetoothDevice, "bluetoothDevice");
    da.i.e(activity, "activity");

    Problem problem = Problem.NO_PROBLEM;

    if (wearableDevice.isWearOSDevice()) {

        if (BluetoothUuidUtil.checkDeviceRegion(activity, bluetoothDevice)) {
            return Problem.WEAR_OS_NOT_SUPPORTED_PHONE;
        }

        if (wearableDevice.isRestoredDevice() && !isConnectedSAKInsecure) {
            BluetoothUuidUtil.isAutoConnectionMode(bluetoothDevice);
        }

    } else if (
        wearableDevice.isEarBudType()
        && PlatformUtils.isSamsungDevice()
        && wearableDevice.hasDeviceId()
        && !BluetoothUuidUtil.isSamsungBudsDevice(bluetoothDevice)
    ) {
        return Problem.FAKE_BUDS;
    }

    return problem;
}
```

The important section was:

```java
if (BluetoothUuidUtil.checkDeviceRegion(activity, bluetoothDevice)) {
    return Problem.WEAR_OS_NOT_SUPPORTED_PHONE;
}
```

