# Then we found the actual region algorithm

`BluetoothUuidUtil.checkDeviceRegion()` contained:

```java
public static boolean checkDeviceRegion(
        Context context,
        BluetoothDevice bluetoothDevice) {

    ResultUUID resultUUIDIsLEChinaModel =
        isLEChinaModel(bluetoothDevice);

    if (resultUUIDIsLEChinaModel == ResultUUID.NULL) {
        b.d(TAG, "checkDeviceRegion, isLEChinaModelUUID is null!!");
        return false;
    }

    boolean z4 =
        resultUUIDIsLEChinaModel == ResultUUID.TRUE;

    boolean zIsChinaEdition =
        GoogleRequirementUtils.isChinaEdition(context);

    b.a(
        TAG,
        "checkDeviceRegion, isWatchChinaModel ["
        + z4
        + "], isPhoneChinaEdition ["
        + zIsChinaEdition
        + "]"
    );

    return zIsChinaEdition ^ z4;
}
```

The final line was the important part:

```java
return zIsChinaEdition ^ z4;
```

That's XOR.

Therefore:

| Phone  | Watch  | Result       |
| ------ | ------ | ------------ |
| Global | Global | Allowed      |
| China  | China  | Allowed      |
| China  | Global | **Rejected** |
| Global | China  | **Rejected** |

Your exact situation was the third row.

